urface":"பிறையென","parts":[{"text":"பிறை","lemma":"பிறை","gloss":"crescent moon"},{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like crescent moon"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மதிமயக்","parts":[{"text":"மதிமயக்","lemma":"மதிமயக்","gloss":"moon-confusing"}],"gloss":"moon-confusing","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"குறூஉ","parts":[{"text":"குறூஉ","lemma":"குறூஉ","gloss":"causing"}],"gloss":"causing","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நுதலு","parts":[{"text":"நுதலு","lemma":"நுதலு","gloss":"forehead also"}],"gloss":"forehead also","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நன்றும்","parts":[{"text":"நன்று","lemma":"நன்று","gloss":"very"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"very indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நல்லமன்","parts":[{"text":"நல்ல","lemma":"நல்ல","gloss":"good"},{"text":"மன்","lemma":"மன்","gloss":"indeed (past state)"}],"gloss":"were indeed good"},{"surface":"வாழி","parts":[{"text":"வாழி","lemma":"வாழ்","gloss":"may you live"}],"gloss":"may you live"},{"surface":"தோழி","parts":[{"text":"தோழி","lemma":"தோழி","gloss":"O friend"}],"gloss":"O friend"},{"surface":"அல்கலும்","parts":[{"text":"அல்கல்","lemma":"அல்கல்","gloss":"every day"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"always"}],"gloss":"every day"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தயங்குதிரை","parts":[{"text":"தயங்கு","lemma":"தயங்கு","gloss":"swaying"},{"text":"திரை","lemma":"திரை","gloss":"wave"}],"gloss":"swaying waves"},{"surface":"பொருத","parts":[{"text":"பொருத","lemma":"பொரு","gloss":"dashed against"}],"gloss":"dashed against"},{"surface":"தாழை","parts":[{"text":"தாழை","lemma":"தாழை","gloss":"screw-pine"}],"gloss":"screw-pine"},{"surface":"வெண்பூக்","parts":[{"text":"வெண்பூக்","lemma":"வெண்பூக்","gloss":"white flower"}],"gloss":"white flower","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குருகென","parts":[{"text":"குருகு","lemma":"குருகு","gloss":"heron"},{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like a heron"},{"surface":"மலரும்","parts":[{"text":"மலரும்","lemma":"மலர்","gloss":"blossoming"}],"gloss":"blossoming"},{"surface":"பெருந்துறை","parts":[{"text":"பெருமை","lemma":"பெருமை","gloss":"great"},{"text":"துறை","lemma":"துறை","gloss":"shore"}],"gloss":"great shore"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"விரிநீர்ச்","parts":[{"text":"விரிநீர்ச்","lemma":"விரிநீர்ச்","gloss":"vast water"}],"gloss":"vast water","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சேர்ப்பனொடு","parts":[{"text":"சேர்ப்பன்","lemma":"சேர்ப்பன்","gloss":"lord of the shore"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"ஒடு","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"with the lord of the shore"},{"surface":"நகாஅ","parts":[{"text":"நகாஅ","lemma":"நகாஅ","gloss":"laughing"}],"gloss":"laughing","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வூங்கே","parts":[{"text":"வூங்கே","lemma":"வூங்கே","gloss":"before"}],"gloss":"before","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"With flower resembling eyes also, like bamboo / great beauty attained shoulders also, like crescent moon / moon-confusing causing forehead also, very / were indeed good, may you live, O friend! Every day / swaying waves dashed screw-pine white flower / like a heron blossoming great shore / vast-watered lord of the shore-with, before laughing.","translation":"O friend, may you live! My eyes that resemble flowers, my shoulders that attained the great beauty of bamboo, and my forehead that confuses the crescent moon, were indeed very beautiful, before we laughed in intimacy with the lord of the vast-watered great shore, where the white flowers of the screw-pine, dashed by swaying waves, blossom like herons.","modern":"தோழியே, நீ வாழ்க! அலைகள் மோதும் பெருந்துறையில், தாழையின் வெண்மையான மலர்கள் நாரையைப் போல மலரும் பரந்த நீர்ப்பரப்பைக் கொண்ட கடற்கரைத் தலைவனுடன் நாம் கூடி மகிழ்வதற்கு முன்னால், மலரைப் போன்ற என் கண்களும், மூங்கிலைப் போன்ற அழகு பொருந்திய என் தோள்களும், பிறை நிலவை மயங்கச் செய்யும் என் நெற்றியும் மிகவும் அழகாக இருந்தன.","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her close friend in a state of deep distress due to the hero's absence. She reflects on how beautiful her eyes, shoulders, and forehead used to be before she fell in love and shared intimacy with the lord of the maritime tract. Now, suffering from the pain of separation, her physical beauty has faded, and she has grown pale. The poem uses a vivid image of the neytal landscape: the white flowers of the screw-pine blossoming on the shore look like white herons when struck by the swaying waves. This imagery subtly hints at the deceptive nature of the shore, mirroring how the hero's love, which seemed so comforting, has now brought her grief. Key words like 'nallamaṉ' highlight her regret and the contrast between her past beauty and present state of pining.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}